{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>הִשָּׁבְעָה לִּי בֵּאלֹהִים הֵנָּה אִם תִּשְׁקֹר לִי</b> The word \"אִם\" everywhere introduces an oath; do not think otherwise except in this case, and it occurs in most places of oath-taking: \"אִם תִּשְׁקֹר לִי\"; \"Therefore I have sworn to the house of Eli, אִם יִתְכַּפֵּר עֲוֹן בֵּית עֵלִי\" (1 Samuel 3:14); \"Once I have sworn by My holiness, אִם לְדָוִד אֲכַזֵּב\" (Psalms 89:36); \"אִם יְבוֹאוּן אֶל מְנוּחָתִי\" (ibid. 95:11); \"And he became wrathful and swore, saying, אִם יִרְאֶה אִישׁ בַּאֲנָשִׁים הָאֵלֶּה\" (Deuteronomy 1:34–35). And the matter is that because oaths are in the form of a curse, he says: Swear to me, saying, \"Thus may Elohim do to me and thus add, if you deal falsely with me\" — and so too it says (Genesis 26:28), \"Let there now be an oath (אָלָה) between us,\" and likewise with regard to the supernal: \"I have sworn by My holiness, אִם לְדָוִד אֲכַזֵּב\" (Psalms 89:36), and \"אִם יִתְכַּפֵּר עֲוֹן בֵּית עֵלִי\" (1 Samuel 3:14) — that is, if such should come to pass, my words are not true, and so forth, for He does not wish to state the condition explicitly, and Scripture designates and abbreviates through them. And like them in omitting the condition: (1 Chronicles 4:10) \"And Jabez called to the Elohim of Israel, saying, אִם בָּרֵךְ תְּבָרֲכֵנִי וְהִרְבִּיתָ אֶת גְּבוּלִי … וְעָשִׂיתָ מֵּרָעָה לְבִלְתִּי עָצְבִּי, and Elohim brought about what he asked\" — the condition is omitted entirely; and likewise \"אִם יִרְאוּ אֶת הָאָרֶץ\" (Numbers 14:23) circles back to the first verse, \"As I live, and the glory of YHWH shall fill all the earth\" — and He abbreviates the oath. And the expression \"תִּשְׁקֹר לִי\" is because he is a king and Abraham is a stranger in his land; or it may mean acting falsely in his love, for he was a faithful friend to him, bound to honor him and to do as he pleases — do you not see that he found nothing in him except the matter of the well of water which his servants had seized? Yet he says to him, \"According to the kindness (חֶסֶד) that I have done with you.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:33:07.038920254Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}